{"name":"Kitchen Blue","hex":"#8ab5bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kitchen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A room or area for preparing food.","Cuisine; style of cooking."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To do kitchen work; to prepare food.","To embellish a basic food; to season, add condiments, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitchen"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kitchen","blocks":[{"text":"A kitchen is a room or part of a room used for cooking and food preparation in a dwelling or in a commercial establishment. A modern middle-class residential kitchen is typically equipped with a stove, a sink with hot and cold running water, a refrigerator, and worktops and kitchen cabinets arranged according to a modular design. Many households have a microwave oven, a dishwasher, and other electric appliances. The main functions of a kitchen are to store, prepare and cook food. The room or area may also be used for dining, entertaining and laundry. The design and construction of kitchens is a huge market all over the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/La_cuisine_%28mus%C3%A9e_dart_nouveau%2C_Riga%29_%287563655820%29.jpg/330px-La_cuisine_%28mus%C3%A9e_dart_nouveau%2C_Riga%29_%287563655820%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitchen","wikidata":"Q43164"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Alno_Kuechenzeile_1980er_Jahre.jpg/500px-Alno_Kuechenzeile_1980er_Jahre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Alno_Kuechenzeile_1980er_Jahre.jpg/1280px-Alno_Kuechenzeile_1980er_Jahre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Alno_Kuechenzeile_1980er_Jahre.jpg/500px-Alno_Kuechenzeile_1980er_Jahre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fitted kitchen (Germany, 1980s)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlno_Kuechenzeile_1980er_Jahre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Medieval_kitchen.jpg/500px-Medieval_kitchen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Medieval_kitchen.jpg/500px-Medieval_kitchen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The roasting spit in this European R